# Patch:        030-redirect-neon-intrinsics
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       baby-bear/src/aarch64_neon/packing.rs, baby-bear/src/aarch64_neon/poseidon2.rs, field/src/packed/aarch64_neon.rs, field/src/packed/interleaves.rs, monty-31/src/aarch64_neon/packing.rs, monty-31/src/aarch64_neon/poseidon1.rs, monty-31/src/aarch64_neon/poseidon2.rs, monty-31/src/aarch64_neon/utils.rs
# Hunks:        10
# Class:        cfg-hide
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 210: the `core::arch` intrinsics have no
#               Rust bodies to extract; and 213: aeneas rejects `asm!`.
# Cost:         none in a normal build: every change is behind
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted NEON variants each
#               intrinsic is its model in `arch/` (p3-arch-shims), trusted:
#               reviewed against Arm's pseudocode and tested against the
#               hardware (`arch/tests/neon.rs`). `confuse_compiler`, an
#               optimisation barrier written as an empty `asm!` block, is the
#               identity: a stand-in, listed in TRUST.md.
# Upstreamable: no: the models exist only for the extractor. Models of the
#               intrinsics in the extractor's library, and support for `asm!`,
#               would make it unnecessary.
# Drop when:    the extractor models the `core::arch::aarch64` intrinsics and
#               `asm!`.
# Test:         xcheck p3-baby-bear aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -Ctarget-feature=+neon;
#               xcheck p3-baby-bear aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -Ctarget-feature=+neon --cfg hax_backend_lean
# Mutation:     monty-31's packing imports the models in a normal build, which
#               has no p3-arch-shims dependency, so the aarch64 build fails.
#
# As 020 does for AVX2: every file on BabyBear's NEON path that names a vector
# type or calls an intrinsic imports `core::arch::aarch64` in a normal build and
# `p3_arch_shims::aarch64` under the cfg. The models have the intrinsics' names
# and signatures, over `repr(transparent)` lane arrays, so no other line
# changes. A file that only names `uint32x4_t` or `int32x4_t` is redirected
# too: the types must agree wherever a vector crosses a file. 020 already makes
# p3-arch-shims a dependency of field, monty-31 and baby-bear under the cfg.
# The `#[cfg(test)]` module of field's `aarch64_neon.rs` keeps `core::arch`: it
# is not compiled for extraction.
#
# `confuse_compiler` is `asm!("/*{0:v}*/", inlateout(vreg) x => y, ...)`
# followed by a check that `y == x`: its value is `x`, and its purpose is to
# stop LLVM from rewriting the `vmlsq_u32` that follows it. Under the cfg it is
# the identity, and its two imports, which nothing else uses, are hidden with
# it. The models say nothing about that optimisation; the stand-in is listed in
# TRUST.md.
#
# The tests compile the NEON path for aarch64: as shipped, which can only use
# `core::arch` since p3-arch-shims is not a dependency without the cfg; and
# under the cfg, which shows that the models fit every call site.
#
# Tested:     test-pre-patches.py: 6715 of 6769 upstream tests pass as
#             shipped, 6715 with the pre-patches; 0 divergences from this patch.
#
diff --git a/baby-bear/src/aarch64_neon/packing.rs b/baby-bear/src/aarch64_neon/packing.rs
--- a/baby-bear/src/aarch64_neon/packing.rs
+++ b/baby-bear/src/aarch64_neon/packing.rs
@@ -1,4 +1,8 @@
+// PATCHED: under hax's Lean backend, the lane-array models of the intrinsics.
+#[cfg(not(hax_backend_lean))]
 use core::arch::aarch64::{int32x4_t, uint32x4_t};
+#[cfg(hax_backend_lean)]
+use p3_arch_shims::aarch64::{int32x4_t, uint32x4_t};
 use core::mem::transmute;
 
 use p3_monty_31::{MontyParametersNeon, PackedMontyField31Neon};
